.TH VAULT-LIST 1 "September 2026" "vault" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vault-list \- list files in the vault
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vault list
.RB [ \-\-key
.IR PATH ]
.RB [ \-\-vault
.IR DIR ]
.RI [ PREFIX ]
.br
.B vault ls
\&...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Prints one line per stored file, sorted by name: human-readable size,
modification time (local, minute resolution) and name. With \fIPREFIX\fR only
that file, or files under that folder, are shown. Records the passphrase
cannot open are skipped silently. Takes a shared lock.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-key " PATH"
Key file. Default: $VAULT_KEY, else ~/.vault/key.
.TP
.BI \-\-vault " DIR"
Vault directory. Default: $VAULT_DIR, else ~/.vault/store.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B VAULT_PASSPHRASE
Passphrase, instead of prompting on the terminal.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vault (1),
.BR vault\-get (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Andy Dixon <vault@dixon.cx>, https://www.dixon.cx
